@startuml sequence-transaction-flow
title Fluxo de um lançamento (outbox + event-carried state)

actor Cliente
participant "transaction-service" as TX
database "Outbox (DB)" as OB
participant "Dispatcher" as D
queue "RabbitMQ" as Q
participant "consolidation-service" as CO
database "Consolidation DB" as CDB

Cliente -> TX : POST /transactions
activate TX
TX -> OB : salva Transaction + Outbox (mesma transação)
TX --> Cliente : 201 Created
deactivate TX

D -> OB : lê pendentes (dispatched=false)
D -> Q : publica TransactionRegisteredMessage
D -> OB : marca dispatched=true

Q -> CO : balance_update
activate CO
CO -> CDB : lock + apply(saldo)
deactivate CO

Q -> CO : daily_balance_update
activate CO
CO -> CDB : grava DailyTransaction (idempotente)
deactivate CO

note over Cliente, TX
  O 201 é retornado antes de tocar RabbitMQ/consolidado.
  Por isso lançamentos seguem disponíveis se o consolidado cair (RNF1).
end note

@enduml
